  },
  {
   "n": 15,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>The characteristic equation of a feedback system is s<sup>6</sup> + 2s<sup>5</sup> + 8s<sup>4</sup> + 12s<sup>3</sup> + 20s<sup>2</sup> + 16s + 16 = 0.</p>\n<p><img src=\"media/d5/d58715166a04d5100492.png\"></p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>(a)</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>(b)</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>(c)</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>(d)</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p><img src=\"media/73/73ca726e7798e0a35eaa.png\"></p>\n<p><em>AE </em>order is 4. So, 4 poles are symmetric about origin no sign change below <em>AE</em>. So all 4 poles lie&nbsp;on <em>j</em>&omega;-axis. No sign change above <em>AE</em>. So, both pole in left half of <em>s </em>plane.</p>\n<p><img src=\"media/db/dbbf1cbb50b5101503f4.png\"></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
